From: axon7m bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] audio: default HAL: circuit-switched call audio in the DSP (q6voice)

During a call the audio policy connects Telephony Rx -> earpiece/speaker
and the microphone -> Telephony Tx with device-to-device patches.
ModulePrimary watches setAudioPatch/resetAudioPatch: while such a patch
exists it applies the routes of the patch's devices plus [voice] and holds
the CS-Voice PCM (ro.vendor.audio.voice.card/device) open, which starts
the voice session in the DSP (Linux q6voice); afterwards it closes the
PCMs and applies [voice-off]. No audio data flows through the HAL.
